message.content:
To retrieve the CNAME records for `sample.com` via the VirusTotal API you would:

1. **Get the domain object**  
   ```bash
   curl -X GET \
     https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/sample.com \
     -H "x-apikey: YOUR_API_KEY"
   ```

2. **Inspect the returned JSON** – look under the `"relationships"` section for entries where `"type": "CNAME"`.  
   Each entry will contain an `"id"` field; those are the IDs of the related CNAME objects.

The response will include something like:

```json
{
  "data": {
    "id": "domain_sample_com",
    ...
  },
  "relationships": {
    "cname_records": [
      {"id": "cname_record_abc123"},
      {"id": "cname_record_def456"}
    ]
  }
}
```

So the related object IDs you’re looking for are the values of `"id"` inside the `"cname_records"` array.
